        "Ultimately, Gell and Scarry suggest that phenomenality allows consciousness to extend beyond immediate bodily experience and influence the physical world. Creation represents more than the external expression of an internal state: it involves consciously imagining alternative conditions and materializing them through action. Objects therefore demonstrate how subjective experience becomes consequential beyond the individual, challenging the assumption that human consciousness merely observes a physical reality whose course is already determined."
